concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187a-ss-3c a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "187A(3C) Service providers must keep certain information and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-187a-ss-3c ;
    values:originalText "(3C) If a Bill is introduced into either House of the Parliament that includes an amendment of subsection (3), the Minister:  (a) must refer the amendment to the Parliamentary Joint Committee on Intelligence and Security for review; and  (b) must not in that referral specify, as the period within which the Committee is to report on its review, a period that will end earlier than 15 sitting days of a House of the Parliament after the introduction of the Bill." ;
    skos:definition "(3C) If a Bill is introduced into either House of the Parliament that includes an amendment of subsection (3), the Minister:  (a) must refer the amendment to the Parliamentary Joint Committee on Intelligence and Security for review; and  (b) must not in that referral specify, as the period within which the Committee is to report on its review, a period that will end earlier than 15 sitting days of a House of the Parliament after the introduction of the Bill."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9061571d5e9f4bc7d80887a7e3bc13dad83b5699a4939e05081fe890d3c360a2" ;
