doc:sch-1-sec-187a-ss-3c a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "187A(3C) Service providers must keep certain information and" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3C) If a Bill is introduced into either House of the Parliament that includes an amendment of subsection (3), the Minister:  (a) must refer the amendment to the Parliamentary Joint Committee on Intelligence and Security for review; and  (b) must not in that referral specify, as the period within which the Committee is to report on its review, a period that will end earlier than 15 sitting days of a House of the Parliament after the introduction of the Bill." ;
    cof:pageNumber "16"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187a-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "187A(4) Service providers must keep certain information and"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-187a-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) This section does not require a service provider to keep, or cause to be kept:  (a) information that is the contents or substance of a communication; or Note: This paragraph puts beyond doubt that service providers are not required to keep information about telecommunications content.  (b) information that:  (i) states an address to which a communication was sent on the internet, from a telecommunications device, using an internet access service provided by the service provider; and  (ii) was obtained by the service provider only as a result of providing the service; or Note: This paragraph puts beyond doubt that service providers are not required to keep information about subscribers’ web browsing history.  Chapter 5  Co-operation with agencies" ;
    skos:definition "(4) This section does not require a service provider to keep, or cause to be kept:  (a) information that is the contents or substance of a communication; or Note: This paragraph puts beyond doubt that service providers are not required to keep information about telecommunications content.  (b) information that:  (i) states an address to which a communication was sent on the internet, from a telecommunications device, using an internet access service provided by the service provider; and  (ii) was obtained by the service provider only as a result of providing the service; or Note: This paragraph puts beyond doubt that service providers are not required to keep information about subscribers’ web browsing history.  Chapter 5  Co-operation with agencies"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b91330651eaf6c0e33169939cbe36e798a11faf5545fd252a9307b88e2041d36" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187a ;
    cof:pageNumber "16"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Service providers must keep certain information." ;
    dc:description "(4) This section does not require a service provider to keep, or cause to be kept:" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
