doc:sch-1-sec-187b a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "187B Certain service providers not covered by this Part" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subsection 187A(1) does not apply to a service provider (other than a carrier that is not a carriage service provider) in relation to a relevant service that it operates if:  (a) the service:  (i) is provided only to a person’s immediate circle (within the meaning of section 23 of the Telecommunications Act 1997); or  (ii) is provided only to places that, under section 36 of that Act, are all in the same area; and  (b) the service is not subject to a declaration under subsection (2) of this section.  (2) A Communications Access Coordinator may declare that subsection 187A(1) applies in relation to a relevant service that a service provider operates.  (2A) Before a declaration is made, a Communications Access Coordinator may consult the Privacy Commissioner.  (3) In considering whether to make a declaration, a Communications Access Coordinator must have regard to:  (a) the interests of law enforcement and national security; and  (b) the objects of the Telecommunications Act 1997; and  (ba) the objects of the Privacy Act 1988; and  (bb) any submissions made by the Privacy Commissioner because of the consultation under subsection (2A); and  (c) any other matter that the Coordinator considers relevant.  (4) The declaration must be in writing.  Co-operation with agencies  Chapter 5 Data retention  Part 5-1A Obligation to keep information and documents  Division 1  Section 187BA  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (5) A declaration made under subsection (2) is not a legislative instrument.  (6) As soon as practicable after a declaration is made under subsection (2), a Communications Access Coordinator must give written notice of the declaration to the Minister.  (7) As soon as practicable after receiving the notice under subsection (6), the Minister must give written notice of the declaration to the Parliamentary Joint Committee on Intelligence and Security." ;
    cof:pageNumber "22"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187b-ss-1 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "187B(1) Certain service providers not covered by this Part"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-187b-ss-1 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Subsection 187A(1) does not apply to a service provider (other than a carrier that is not a carriage service provider) in relation to a relevant service that it operates if:  (a) the service:  (i) is provided only to a person’s immediate circle (within the meaning of section 23 of the Telecommunications Act 1997); or  (ii) is provided only to places that, under section 36 of that Act, are all in the same area; and  (b) the service is not subject to a declaration under subsection (2) of this section." ;
    skos:definition "(1) Subsection 187A(1) does not apply to a service provider (other than a carrier that is not a carriage service provider) in relation to a relevant service that it operates if:  (a) the service:  (i) is provided only to a person’s immediate circle (within the meaning of section 23 of the Telecommunications Act 1997); or  (ii) is provided only to places that, under section 36 of that Act, are all in the same area; and  (b) the service is not subject to a declaration under subsection (2) of this section."@en ;
