concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187b-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "187B(3) Certain service providers not covered by this Part"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-187b-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) In considering whether to make a declaration, a Communications Access Coordinator must have regard to:  (a) the interests of law enforcement and national security; and  (b) the objects of the Telecommunications Act 1997; and  (ba) the objects of the Privacy Act 1988; and  (bb) any submissions made by the Privacy Commissioner because of the consultation under subsection (2A); and  (c) any other matter that the Coordinator considers relevant." ;
    skos:definition "(3) In considering whether to make a declaration, a Communications Access Coordinator must have regard to:  (a) the interests of law enforcement and national security; and  (b) the objects of the Telecommunications Act 1997; and  (ba) the objects of the Privacy Act 1988; and  (bb) any submissions made by the Privacy Commissioner because of the consultation under subsection (2A); and  (c) any other matter that the Coordinator considers relevant."@en ;
