concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187k a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "187K Communications Access Coordinator may grant exemptions"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-187k ;
    values:originalText "or variations Decision to exempt or vary  (1) A Communications Access Coordinator may:  (a) exempt a specified service provider from the obligations imposed on the service provider under this Part, either generally or in so far as they relate to a specified kind of relevant service; or  (b) vary the obligations imposed on a specified service provider under this Part, either generally or in so far as they relate to a specified kind of relevant service; or  (c) vary, in relation to a specified service provider, a period specified in section 187C, either generally or in relation to information or documents that relate to a specified kind of relevant service. A variation must not impose obligations that would exceed the obligations to which a service provider would otherwise be subject under sections 187A and 187C.  (2) The decision must be in writing.  (3) The decision may be:  (a) unconditional; or  (b) subject to such conditions as are specified in the decision.  (4) A decision made under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument. Effect of applying for exemption or variation  (5) If a service provider applies in writing to a Communications Access Coordinator for a particular decision under subsection (1) relating to the service provider:  Chapter 5  Co-operation with agencies" ;
    skos:definition "or variations Decision to exempt or vary  (1) A Communications Access Coordinator may:  (a) exempt a specified service provider from the obligations imposed on the service provider under this Part, either generally or in so far as they relate to a specified kind of relevant service; or  (b) vary the obligations imposed on a specified service provider under this Part, either generally or in so far as they relate to a specified kind of relevant service; or  (c) vary, in relation to a specified service provider, a period specified in section 187C, either generally or in relation to information or documents that relate to a specified kind of relevant service. A variation must not impose obligations that would exceed the obligations to which a service provider would otherwise be subject under sections 187A and 187C.  (2) The decision must be in writing.  (3) The decision may be:  (a) unconditional; or  (b) subject to such conditions as are specified in the decision.  (4) A decision made under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument. Effect of applying for exemption or variation  (5) If a service provider applies in writing to a Communications Access Coordinator for a particular decision under subsection (1) relating to the service provider:  Chapter 5  Co-operation with agencies"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a1e424755443e90c0fb7eaf3db20eb7e510931c1fc283f9d21df40c2ade621ee" ;
    cof:pageNumber "31"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187k-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187k-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-187k-ss-3 ;
