    skos:definition "(1) A Communications Access Coordinator may:  (a) exempt a specified service provider from the obligations imposed on the service provider under this Part, either generally or in so far as they relate to a specified kind of relevant service; or  (b) vary the obligations imposed on a specified service provider under this Part, either generally or in so far as they relate to a specified kind of relevant service; or  (c) vary, in relation to a specified service provider, a period specified in section 187C, either generally or in relation to information or documents that relate to a specified kind of relevant service. A variation must not impose obligations that would exceed the obligations to which a service provider would otherwise be subject under sections 187A and 187C."@en ;
