concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-188 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "188 Delivery points"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-188 ;
    values:originalText "(1) Each carrier must:  (a) nominate, in respect of a particular kind of telecommunications service of that carrier and in respect of each interception agency, at least one place in Australia as the location of a point from which lawfully intercepted information can most conveniently be transmitted in relation to that interception agency; and  (b) inform a Communications Access Coordinator of the place or places nominated for each interception agency. Note 1: The nominated location becomes a delivery point: see the definition of delivery point in subsection 5(1). Note 2: The definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service providers. Note 3: Delivery points are significant for the interception capability obligations in Part 5-3 and for the delivery capability obligations in" ;
    skos:definition "(1) Each carrier must:  (a) nominate, in respect of a particular kind of telecommunications service of that carrier and in respect of each interception agency, at least one place in Australia as the location of a point from which lawfully intercepted information can most conveniently be transmitted in relation to that interception agency; and  (b) inform a Communications Access Coordinator of the place or places nominated for each interception agency. Note 1: The nominated location becomes a delivery point: see the definition of delivery point in subsection 5(1). Note 2: The definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service providers. Note 3: Delivery points are significant for the interception capability obligations in Part 5-3 and for the delivery capability obligations in"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "d7a166b8e86cad0c97d131daa2c64f975fca05f94e0c7d42bc73c88ed4f87453" ;
    cof:pageNumber "39"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Carrier must nominate a location for transmission of intercepted information." ;
    dc:description "true" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.39" ;
    cml:asserts concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-188-norm .
