concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-190 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "190 Obligations of persons covered by a determination"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-190 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a determination under section 189 applies to a particular kind of telecommunications service that involves, or will involve, the use of a telecommunications system, each carrier supplying that kind of service must comply with the determination. Note: The definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service providers.  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a carrier is required to have interception capability in relation to a particular kind of telecommunications service under the determination, the carrier is required to ensure that the capability is developed, installed and maintained. Note 1: A person may be exempted from the requirements of this section under a provision of Division 2. Note 2: The cost of this capability is to be borne by the carriers: see Division 2 of Part 5-6." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If a determination under section 189 applies to a particular kind of telecommunications service that involves, or will involve, the use of a telecommunications system, each carrier supplying that kind of service must comply with the determination. Note: The definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service providers.  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a carrier is required to have interception capability in relation to a particular kind of telecommunications service under the determination, the carrier is required to ensure that the capability is developed, installed and maintained. Note 1: A person may be exempted from the requirements of this section under a provision of Division 2. Note 2: The cost of this capability is to be borne by the carriers: see Division 2 of Part 5-6."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "e2fe0107a2fecfea077375ba340c92c8a383da37e4c40067123bd247415a62e3" ;
    cof:pageNumber "43"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-190-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-190-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.43" .
doc:sch-1-sec-190 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "190 Obligations of persons covered by a determination" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a determination under section 189 applies to a particular kind of telecommunications service that involves, or will involve, the use of a telecommunications system, each carrier supplying that kind of service must comply with the determination. Note: The definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service providers.  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a carrier is required to have interception capability in relation to a particular kind of telecommunications service under the determination, the carrier is required to ensure that the capability is developed, installed and maintained. Note 1: A person may be exempted from the requirements of this section under a provision of Division 2. Note 2: The cost of this capability is to be borne by the carriers: see Division 2 of Part 5-6." ;
    cof:pageNumber "43"^^xsd:integer .

