concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-196 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "196 Time for giving IC plans by carriers"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-196 ;
    values:originalText "(1) A carrier must give an IC plan to a Communications Access Coordinator by:  (a) each 1 July; or  (b) if a Communications Access Coordinator agrees to a later day instead of a particular 1 July—that later day. Note: If the business plans of the carrier change, the carrier may be required to give a Communications Access Coordinator another IC plan under section 201.  (2) A Communications Access Coordinator must inform the ACMA of any agreement under paragraph (1)(b). Further rule for future carriers  (3) If the carrier became a carrier on a day (the start day) after the commencement of this section, the carrier must also give an IC plan to a Communications Access Coordinator within 90 days after the start day." ;
    skos:definition "(1) A carrier must give an IC plan to a Communications Access Coordinator by:  (a) each 1 July; or  (b) if a Communications Access Coordinator agrees to a later day instead of a particular 1 July—that later day. Note: If the business plans of the carrier change, the carrier may be required to give a Communications Access Coordinator another IC plan under section 201.  (2) A Communications Access Coordinator must inform the ACMA of any agreement under paragraph (1)(b). Further rule for future carriers  (3) If the carrier became a carrier on a day (the start day) after the commencement of this section, the carrier must also give an IC plan to a Communications Access Coordinator within 90 days after the start day."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "bf038c1e91586ffa07535855b9186b262460facd415c2c6027b3cfc0ac592058" ;
    cof:pageNumber "48"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-196-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-196-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-196-ss-3 ;
