doc:sch-1-sec-202 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "202 Confidential treatment of IC plans" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Once a Communications Access Coordinator, the ACMA or an interception agency receives an IC plan of a carrier or nominated carriage service provider, the Coordinator, the ACMA or the interception agency:  (a) must treat the plan as confidential; and  (b) must ensure that it is not disclosed to any person or body not referred to in this section without the written permission of the carrier or provider.  Chapter 5  Co-operation with agencies" ;
