concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-204 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "204 Obligations of persons covered by a determination"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-204 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If a determination under section 203 applies:  (a) to a particular kind of telecommunications service that involves, or will involve, the use of a telecommunications system; and  (b) to a carrier; the carrier must comply with the determination. Note: The definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service providers.  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a carrier is required to have delivery capability in relation to a particular kind of telecommunications service under the determination, the carrier is required to ensure that the capability is developed, installed and maintained. Note: The cost of this capability is to be borne by the interception agencies: see Division 3 of Part 5-6." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If a determination under section 203 applies:  (a) to a particular kind of telecommunications service that involves, or will involve, the use of a telecommunications system; and  (b) to a carrier; the carrier must comply with the determination. Note: The definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service providers.  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), if a carrier is required to have delivery capability in relation to a particular kind of telecommunications service under the determination, the carrier is required to ensure that the capability is developed, installed and maintained. Note: The cost of this capability is to be borne by the interception agencies: see Division 3 of Part 5-6."@en ;
