    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "relation to a kind of telecommunications service  (1) Each carrier supplying a particular kind of telecommunications service that is not covered by any determination under section 203 but that involves, or will involve, the use of a telecommunications system must ensure that the kind of service or the system has a delivery capability. Note: The definition of carrier in subsection 5(1) includes carriage service providers.  (2) Without limiting subsection (1), the obligation under that subsection includes the obligation to ensure that the capability is developed, installed and maintained. Note: The cost of this capability is to be borne by the interception agencies: see Division 3 of Part 5-6.  Co-operation with agencies  Chapter 5 Allocation of costs  Part 5-6 Outline of Part  Division 1  Section 206  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
