    values:originalText "(4) If:  (a) notice of a motion to disallow the regulations is given in a House of the Parliament within 15 sitting days of that House  International production orders  Schedule 1 Introduction  Part 1  Clause 3B  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  after the copy of the regulations was tabled in that House under section 38 of the Legislation Act 2003; and  (b) at the end of 15 sitting days of that House after the giving of that notice of motion:  (i) the notice has not been withdrawn and the motion has not been called on; or  (ii) the motion has been called on, moved and (where relevant) seconded and has not been withdrawn or otherwise disposed of; the regulations is then taken to have been disallowed, and subclause (3) does not apply to the regulations." ;
    cof:pageNumber "84"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3a-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3A(5) Disallowance of regulations relating to designated international"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-3a-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) Section 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not apply to the regulations. Note 1: The 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in paragraph (2)(a) of this clause is the same as the 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in paragraph 42(1)(a) of the Legislation Act 2003. Note 2: The 15 sitting day disallowance period mentioned in paragraph (2)(b) of this clause is the same as the 15 sitting day disallowance period mentioned in paragraph 42(1)(b) of the Legislation Act 2003." ;
    skos:definition "(5) Section 42 (disallowance) of the Legislation Act 2003 does not apply to the regulations. Note 1: The 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in paragraph (2)(a) of this clause is the same as the 15 sitting day notice period mentioned in paragraph 42(1)(a) of the Legislation Act 2003. Note 2: The 15 sitting day disallowance period mentioned in paragraph (2)(b) of this clause is the same as the 15 sitting day disallowance period mentioned in paragraph 42(1)(b) of the Legislation Act 2003."@en ;
