concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-3b a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "3B Statutory requirements certificate—designated international"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-3b ;
    values:originalText "agreements Scope  (1) This section applies if:  (a) there is an agreement between Australia and one or more foreign countries; and  (b) the agreement deals with (among other things) the issue of orders (however described) by a competent authority (however described) of the foreign country, or each of the foreign countries, concerned.  Schedule 1  International production orders" ;
    skos:definition "agreements Scope  (1) This section applies if:  (a) there is an agreement between Australia and one or more foreign countries; and  (b) the agreement deals with (among other things) the issue of orders (however described) by a competent authority (however described) of the foreign country, or each of the foreign countries, concerned.  Schedule 1  International production orders"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "05c56afe6460bebd9580d2b8ee3b5d1b054a8898f95a4343bf6afce47f1e29c5" ;
    cof:pageNumber "85"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Statutory requirements for international agreements regarding orders by a competent authority of a foreign country." ;
