doc:sch-1-sec-13 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "13 Identification of a particular person" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "For the purposes of this Schedule, a particular person may be identified:  (a) by the person’s full name; or  (b) by a name by which the person is commonly known; or  International production orders  Schedule 1 Introduction  Part 1  Clause 14  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (c) as the person to whom a particular individual transmission service is supplied; or  (d) as the person to whom a particular individual message/call application service is provided; or  (e) as the person who has a particular account with a prescribed communications provider; or  (f) as the person who has a particular telephone number; or  (g) as the person who has a particular email address; or  (h) as the person who has a particular internet protocol address; or  (i) as the person who has a device that has a particular unique identifier (for example, an electronic serial number or a Media Access Control address); or  (j) by any other unique identifying factor that is applicable to the person." ;
    cof:pageNumber "92"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-14 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "14 Eligible judge"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-14 ;
    values:originalText "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, eligible Judge means a person:  (a) in relation to whom a consent under subclause (2) and a declaration under subclause (3) are in force; and  (b) in relation to an international production order applied for by the National Anti-Corruption Commission—who is a superior Court Judge.  (2) A Judge may, by writing, consent to be nominated by the Attorney-General under subclause (3).  (3) The Attorney-General may, by writing, declare Judges in relation to whom consents are in force under subclause (2) to be eligible Judges for the purposes of this Schedule.  (4) An eligible Judge has, in relation to the performance or exercise of a function or power conferred on an eligible Judge by this Schedule, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court.  Schedule 1  International production orders" ;
    skos:definition "(1) For the purposes of this Schedule, eligible Judge means a person:  (a) in relation to whom a consent under subclause (2) and a declaration under subclause (3) are in force; and  (b) in relation to an international production order applied for by the National Anti-Corruption Commission—who is a superior Court Judge.  (2) A Judge may, by writing, consent to be nominated by the Attorney-General under subclause (3).  (3) The Attorney-General may, by writing, declare Judges in relation to whom consents are in force under subclause (2) to be eligible Judges for the purposes of this Schedule.  (4) An eligible Judge has, in relation to the performance or exercise of a function or power conferred on an eligible Judge by this Schedule, the same protection and immunity as a Justice of the High Court has in relation to proceedings in the High Court.  Schedule 1  International production orders"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "426a901ee39dd821a6c4eb1d26098deb28f4253b64b21f564b0dc79f02ffbdc7" ;
    cof:pageNumber "93"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-14-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-14-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-14-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-14-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.93" .
