doc:sch-1-sec-35 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "35 Contents of written application" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "An application under clause 33 must, if it is in writing, set out:  (a) the name of the criminal law-enforcement agency; and  (b) the name of the person making the application on the agency’s behalf." ;
    cof:pageNumber "120"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-36 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "36 Affidavits to accompany written application"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-36 ;
    values:originalText "(1) An application under clause 33 must, if it is in writing, be accompanied by an affidavit complying with this clause.  (2) The affidavit must set out the facts and other grounds on which the application is based.  (3) Despite subclause (1), a written application may be accompanied by 2 or more affidavits that together set out each matter that, apart from this subclause, this clause would have required an affidavit accompanying the application to set out.  International production orders  Schedule 1 International production orders relating to the enforcement of the criminal law  Part 2 International production orders relating to stored communications: enforcement of the criminal law  Division 3  Clause 37  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(1) An application under clause 33 must, if it is in writing, be accompanied by an affidavit complying with this clause.  (2) The affidavit must set out the facts and other grounds on which the application is based.  (3) Despite subclause (1), a written application may be accompanied by 2 or more affidavits that together set out each matter that, apart from this subclause, this clause would have required an affidavit accompanying the application to set out.  International production orders  Schedule 1 International production orders relating to the enforcement of the criminal law  Part 2 International production orders relating to stored communications: enforcement of the criminal law  Division 3  Clause 37  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
