concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-42 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "42 Application for international production order—enforcement of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-42 ;
    values:originalText "the criminal law  (1) An enforcement agency may apply to an issuing authority for an international production order under clause 48 that is directed to a prescribed communications provider.  (2) The application must nominate a designated international agreement.  (3) The application must be made on the enforcement agency’s behalf by an authorised officer of the agency." ;
    skos:definition "the criminal law  (1) An enforcement agency may apply to an issuing authority for an international production order under clause 48 that is directed to a prescribed communications provider.  (2) The application must nominate a designated international agreement.  (3) The application must be made on the enforcement agency’s behalf by an authorised officer of the agency."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "89a1420b145908bae01e953e6f597567f43eb5d11b77ff56043c7b3042a442dd" ;
    cof:pageNumber "128"^^xsd:integer ;
