    values:originalText "(1) An application under clause 42 must be in writing.  (2) However, a person making the application on the enforcement agency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the person:  (a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to whom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under subclause (3); and  (b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make the application by telephone. Note: See also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action required).  (3) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may, in writing, authorise persons (including classes of persons) for the purposes of  International production orders  Schedule 1 International production orders relating to the enforcement of the criminal law  Part 2 International production orders relating to telecommunications data: enforcement of the criminal law  Division 4  Clause 44  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  subclause (2). However, each person must be entitled under clause 42 to make applications on the agency’s behalf." ;
    skos:definition "(1) An application under clause 42 must be in writing.  (2) However, a person making the application on the enforcement agency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the person:  (a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to whom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under subclause (3); and  (b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make the application by telephone. Note: See also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action required).  (3) The chief officer of an enforcement agency may, in writing, authorise persons (including classes of persons) for the purposes of  International production orders  Schedule 1 International production orders relating to the enforcement of the criminal law  Part 2 International production orders relating to telecommunications data: enforcement of the criminal law  Division 4  Clause 44  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  subclause (2). However, each person must be entitled under clause 42 to make applications on the agency’s behalf."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "9a65297aca79ded5b16d9d6c1cb562799878ee47470212ea9ced2e1b3f18166c" ;
