concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-73 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "73 Form of application"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-73 ;
    values:originalText "(1) An application under clause 72 must be in writing.  (2) However, a person making the application on the Part 5.3 IPO agency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the person:  (a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to whom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under subclause (3); and  (b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make the application by telephone. Note: See also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action required).  Schedule 1  International production orders" ;
    skos:definition "(1) An application under clause 72 must be in writing.  (2) However, a person making the application on the Part 5.3 IPO agency’s behalf may make the application by telephone if the person:  (a) is the chief officer of the agency or a person in relation to whom an authorisation by the chief officer is in force under subclause (3); and  (b) thinks it necessary, because of urgent circumstances, to make the application by telephone. Note: See also clause 17A (urgent circumstances) and clause 172 (action required).  Schedule 1  International production orders"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "eda46d348feca1e5c7b18ed03a268a684ac1598700b961793d64f1c6f6424c23" ;
    cof:pageNumber "167"^^xsd:integer ;
