doc:sch-1-sec-80 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "80 Issue of further international production order" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If:  (a) an international production order (the original order) was issued under clause 78; and  (b) the original order was in respect of a particular person; and  (c) the original order was directed to a prescribed communications provider; this Schedule does not prevent the issue of a further international production order under clause 78 that:  (d) is in respect of the person; and  (e) is directed to the provider.  International production orders  Schedule 1 International production orders relating to Part 5.3 supervisory orders  Part 3 Notification to Ombudsman or the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security by" ;
    cof:pageNumber "174"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-81 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "81 Notification to Ombudsman or the Inspector-General of"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-81 ;
    values:originalText "Intelligence and Security by Part 5.3 IPO agencies in relation to international production orders  (1) Within 3 months after an international production order is issued under this Part in response to an application by a Part 5.3 IPO agency, the chief officer of the agency must:  (a) if the agency is the ACC:  (i) notify the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security that the order has been issued; and  (ii) give to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security a copy of the order; and  (b) otherwise:  (i) notify the Ombudsman that the order has been issued; and  (ii) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the order.  (2) If the chief officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency contravenes paragraph 114(1)(d) of this Schedule (so far as that paragraph relates to an international production order issued under this Part), the chief officer must:  (a) notify the Ombudsman or the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security (as the case requires) of the contravention; and  (b) do so as soon as practicable after the contravention.  (3) A failure to comply with subclause (1) or (2) does not affect the validity of an international production order.  Schedule 1  International production orders" ;
    skos:definition "Intelligence and Security by Part 5.3 IPO agencies in relation to international production orders  (1) Within 3 months after an international production order is issued under this Part in response to an application by a Part 5.3 IPO agency, the chief officer of the agency must:  (a) if the agency is the ACC:  (i) notify the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security that the order has been issued; and  (ii) give to the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security a copy of the order; and  (b) otherwise:  (i) notify the Ombudsman that the order has been issued; and  (ii) give to the Ombudsman a copy of the order.  (2) If the chief officer of a Part 5.3 IPO agency contravenes paragraph 114(1)(d) of this Schedule (so far as that paragraph relates to an international production order issued under this Part), the chief officer must:  (a) notify the Ombudsman or the Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security (as the case requires) of the contravention; and  (b) do so as soon as practicable after the contravention.  (3) A failure to comply with subclause (1) or (2) does not affect the validity of an international production order.  Schedule 1  International production orders"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "a44bf1448f62c4fe96600d9a38105fd33cc1b4c63eff44afc596c43ac6d75126" ;
    cof:pageNumber "175"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-81-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-81-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-81-ss-3 ;
