concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-82 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "82 Simplified outline of this Part"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-82 ;
    values:originalText "• International production orders may be issued for purposes in connection with the carrying out by the Organisation of its functions. • There are 3 types of international production orders:  (a) international production orders relating to interception; and  (b) international production orders relating to stored communications; and  (c) international production orders relating to telecommunications data. • An international production order is directed to a prescribed communications provider. • An international production order may be issued in response to an application made by the Organisation. • An application for an international production order must nominate a designated international agreement. Note: An international production order comes into force when it is given to a prescribed communications provider under clause 112.  International production orders  Schedule 1 International production orders relating to national security  Part 4 International production orders relating to interception: national security  Division 2  Clause 83  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "• International production orders may be issued for purposes in connection with the carrying out by the Organisation of its functions. • There are 3 types of international production orders:  (a) international production orders relating to interception; and  (b) international production orders relating to stored communications; and  (c) international production orders relating to telecommunications data. • An international production order is directed to a prescribed communications provider. • An international production order may be issued in response to an application made by the Organisation. • An application for an international production order must nominate a designated international agreement. Note: An international production order comes into force when it is given to a prescribed communications provider under clause 112.  International production orders  Schedule 1 International production orders relating to national security  Part 4 International production orders relating to interception: national security  Division 2  Clause 83  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "cabdebb20bc29657fb6fd2d60b3196ca38e07a605c6beb06fc06249da7181294" ;
    cof:pageNumber "176"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "International production orders may be issued for purposes in connection with the carrying out by the Organisation of its functions." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
