    cof:title "100 Issue of further international production order" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "If:  (a) an international production order (the original order) was issued under clause 98; and  (b) the original order was in respect of a particular person; and  (c) the original order was directed to a prescribed communications provider; this Schedule does not prevent the issue of a further international production order under clause 98 that:  (d) is in respect of the person; and  (e) is directed to the provider.  International production orders  Schedule 1 International production orders relating to national security  Part 4 International production orders relating to telecommunications data: national security" ;
    cof:pageNumber "202"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-101 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "101 Application for international production order—national"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-101 ;
    values:originalText "security  (1) The Organisation may apply to a nominated ART Intelligence and Security member for an international production order under clause 107 that:  (a) is in respect of a particular person; and  (b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.  (2) The application must nominate a designated international agreement.  (3) The application must be made on the Organisation’s behalf by:  (a) the Director-General of Security; or  (b) a Deputy Director-General of Security; or  (c) an eligible position-holder in relation to whom an authorisation is in force under subclause (4).  (4) The Director-General of Security may authorise in writing, for the purposes of subclause (3), eligible position-holders who, or classes of eligible position-holders who, are entitled under subclause (1) to make applications on the Organisation’s behalf." ;
    skos:definition "security  (1) The Organisation may apply to a nominated ART Intelligence and Security member for an international production order under clause 107 that:  (a) is in respect of a particular person; and  (b) is directed to a prescribed communications provider.  (2) The application must nominate a designated international agreement.  (3) The application must be made on the Organisation’s behalf by:  (a) the Director-General of Security; or  (b) a Deputy Director-General of Security; or  (c) an eligible position-holder in relation to whom an authorisation is in force under subclause (4).  (4) The Director-General of Security may authorise in writing, for the purposes of subclause (3), eligible position-holders who, or classes of eligible position-holders who, are entitled under subclause (1) to make applications on the Organisation’s behalf."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "5d2d3ceb7abe552344276d47d36a8175b7aeb250a9bf0bf00e850cd23ecf2e43" ;
    cof:pageNumber "203"^^xsd:integer ;
