concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-117 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "117 Giving of instrument of revocation—the Organisation"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-117 ;
    values:originalText "(1) If an international production order is revoked under clause 116 by the Director-General of Security, the Organisation must:  (a) give the instrument of revocation to the Australian Designated Authority; and  (b) do so as soon as practicable after the order is revoked.  International production orders  Schedule 1 Revocation of international production orders  Part 6  Clause 118  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (2) If:  (a) the Australian Designated Authority gave an international production order to the prescribed communications provider to whom the order is directed; and  (b) the order was subsequently revoked under clause 116; the Australian Designated Authority must:  (c) give the instrument of revocation to the prescribed communications provider; and  (d) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of revocation is given to the Australian Designated Authority.  (3) A revocation under clause 116 takes effect:  (a) if the instrument of revocation is required to be given to the prescribed communications provider concerned—when the instrument is given; or  (b) otherwise—when the revocation is made.  (4) If:  (a) an international production order is revoked under clause 116; and  (b) when the revocation takes effect, the Australian Designated Authority has not made a decision about the order under clause 112; clause 112 ceases to apply to the order when the revocation takes effect." ;
    skos:definition "(1) If an international production order is revoked under clause 116 by the Director-General of Security, the Organisation must:  (a) give the instrument of revocation to the Australian Designated Authority; and  (b) do so as soon as practicable after the order is revoked.  International production orders  Schedule 1 Revocation of international production orders  Part 6  Clause 118  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (2) If:  (a) the Australian Designated Authority gave an international production order to the prescribed communications provider to whom the order is directed; and  (b) the order was subsequently revoked under clause 116; the Australian Designated Authority must:  (c) give the instrument of revocation to the prescribed communications provider; and  (d) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of revocation is given to the Australian Designated Authority.  (3) A revocation under clause 116 takes effect:  (a) if the instrument of revocation is required to be given to the prescribed communications provider concerned—when the instrument is given; or  (b) otherwise—when the revocation is made.  (4) If:  (a) an international production order is revoked under clause 116; and  (b) when the revocation takes effect, the Australian Designated Authority has not made a decision about the order under clause 112; clause 112 ceases to apply to the order when the revocation takes effect."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "fd1729621342bd406acf68cf2d08fd6cc9f3dce53a6ce36705e545a3ccf3894a" ;
    cof:pageNumber "218"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-117-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-117-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-117-ss-3 ;
