concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-118 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "118 Delegation by the chief officer of a relevant agency"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-118 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The chief officer of a relevant agency may, by writing, delegate any or all of the chief officer’s functions or powers under this Part to a certifying officer of the agency.  (2) In performing functions, or exercising powers, under a delegation under subclause (1), the delegate must comply with any directions of the chief officer.  Schedule 1  International production orders" ;
    skos:definition "(1) The chief officer of a relevant agency may, by writing, delegate any or all of the chief officer’s functions or powers under this Part to a certifying officer of the agency.  (2) In performing functions, or exercising powers, under a delegation under subclause (1), the delegate must comply with any directions of the chief officer.  Schedule 1  International production orders"@en ;
