concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-119 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "119 Delegation by the Director-General of Security"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-119 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Director-General of Security may, by writing, delegate any or all of the Director-General of Security’s functions or powers under this Part to a person who is:  (a) a Deputy Director-General of Security; or  (b) an ASIO employee.  (2) In performing functions, or exercising powers, under a delegation under subclause (1), the delegate must comply with any directions of the Director-General of Security.  International production orders  Schedule 1 Objections to, and cancellation of, international production orders  Part 7  Clause 120  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
