    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(5) Part 4 of the Regulatory Powers (Standard Provisions) Act 2014, as it applies in relation to a civil penalty provision in this Part, extends to acts, omissions, matters and things outside Australia.  International production orders  Schedule 1 Reporting and record-keeping requirements  Part 9 Introduction  Division 1  Clause 127  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    cof:pageNumber "226"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-127 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "127 Simplified outline of this Part"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-127 ;
    values:originalText "• The chief officer of a relevant agency and the Australian Designated Authority must give the Minister annual reports about matters relating to international production orders. • The Director-General of Security must give the Attorney-General a report on the extent to which compliance by a prescribed communications provider with an international production order has assisted the Organisation in carrying out its functions. • The Minister must cause to be prepared annual reports about matters relating to international production orders that were issued in response to applications made by relevant agencies. • The chief officer of a relevant agency, the Director-General of Security and the Australian Designated Authority must ensure that records are kept of matters relating to international production orders.  Schedule 1  International production orders" ;
    skos:definition "• The chief officer of a relevant agency and the Australian Designated Authority must give the Minister annual reports about matters relating to international production orders. • The Director-General of Security must give the Attorney-General a report on the extent to which compliance by a prescribed communications provider with an international production order has assisted the Organisation in carrying out its functions. • The Minister must cause to be prepared annual reports about matters relating to international production orders that were issued in response to applications made by relevant agencies. • The chief officer of a relevant agency, the Director-General of Security and the Australian Designated Authority must ensure that records are kept of matters relating to international production orders.  Schedule 1  International production orders"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "819d7504f4e9b921cf8871100c81885959a44daf664d3e27521e8c76dea7b375" ;
    cof:pageNumber "227"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Annual reports must be given by certain agencies and authorities." ;
    dc:description "annual reports" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.227" ;
