concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-132 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "132 Deferral of inclusion of information in Ministerial report"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-132 ;
    values:originalText "Scope  (1) This clause applies to information:  (a) included in a report given to the Minister:  (i) under clause 128 by the chief officer of a relevant agency; or  (ii) under clause 130 by the Australian Designated Authority; and  International production orders  Schedule 1 Reporting and record-keeping requirements  Part 9 Reporting requirements  Division 2  Clause 132  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) that the Minister would, apart from this clause, be required to include in the next Ministerial report. Exclusion of information—relevant agency  (2) If:  (a) subparagraph (1)(a)(i) applies; and  (b) the chief officer of the relevant agency is satisfied that the information is Part 5.3 information; the chief officer must advise the Minister in writing not to include the information in the next Ministerial report.  (3) If the Minister is satisfied, on the advice of the chief officer, that the information is Part 5.3 information, the Minister must:  (a) notify the chief officer in writing; and  (b) not include the information in any Ministerial report until the Minister decides otherwise under subclause (5). Inclusion of information in subsequent report—relevant agency  (4) If the information has not been included in a Ministerial report because of subclause (3), the chief officer must, before the Minister prepares the next Ministerial report:  (a) reconsider whether the information is Part 5.3 information; and  (b) if the chief officer is satisfied that the information is not" ;
    skos:definition "Scope  (1) This clause applies to information:  (a) included in a report given to the Minister:  (i) under clause 128 by the chief officer of a relevant agency; or  (ii) under clause 130 by the Australian Designated Authority; and  International production orders  Schedule 1 Reporting and record-keeping requirements  Part 9 Reporting requirements  Division 2  Clause 132  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) that the Minister would, apart from this clause, be required to include in the next Ministerial report. Exclusion of information—relevant agency  (2) If:  (a) subparagraph (1)(a)(i) applies; and  (b) the chief officer of the relevant agency is satisfied that the information is Part 5.3 information; the chief officer must advise the Minister in writing not to include the information in the next Ministerial report.  (3) If the Minister is satisfied, on the advice of the chief officer, that the information is Part 5.3 information, the Minister must:  (a) notify the chief officer in writing; and  (b) not include the information in any Ministerial report until the Minister decides otherwise under subclause (5). Inclusion of information in subsequent report—relevant agency  (4) If the information has not been included in a Ministerial report because of subclause (3), the chief officer must, before the Minister prepares the next Ministerial report:  (a) reconsider whether the information is Part 5.3 information; and  (b) if the chief officer is satisfied that the information is not"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "b073f6c68ef8721107fd9815b19b2c35ec111d526b75c2123d1111ba64424000" ;
    cof:pageNumber "232"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-132-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-132-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-132-ss-3 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-132-ss-4 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf> ;
    dc:source "telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf, p.232" .
doc:sch-1-sec-132 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "132 Deferral of inclusion of information in Ministerial report" ;
    values:kind "section" ;
    values:originalText "Scope  (1) This clause applies to information:  (a) included in a report given to the Minister:  (i) under clause 128 by the chief officer of a relevant agency; or  (ii) under clause 130 by the Australian Designated Authority; and  International production orders  Schedule 1 Reporting and record-keeping requirements  Part 9 Reporting requirements  Division 2  Clause 132  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) that the Minister would, apart from this clause, be required to include in the next Ministerial report. Exclusion of information—relevant agency  (2) If:  (a) subparagraph (1)(a)(i) applies; and  (b) the chief officer of the relevant agency is satisfied that the information is Part 5.3 information; the chief officer must advise the Minister in writing not to include the information in the next Ministerial report.  (3) If the Minister is satisfied, on the advice of the chief officer, that the information is Part 5.3 information, the Minister must:  (a) notify the chief officer in writing; and  (b) not include the information in any Ministerial report until the Minister decides otherwise under subclause (5). Inclusion of information in subsequent report—relevant agency  (4) If the information has not been included in a Ministerial report because of subclause (3), the chief officer must, before the Minister prepares the next Ministerial report:  (a) reconsider whether the information is Part 5.3 information; and  (b) if the chief officer is satisfied that the information is not" ;
    cof:pageNumber "232"^^xsd:integer .

