concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-133 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "133 Keeping documents associated with international production"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-133 ;
    values:originalText "orders—relevant agencies  (1) The chief officer of a relevant agency must cause the following to be kept in the agency’s records:  (a) a copy of each written application made by the agency for an international production order;  (b) a copy of each affidavit that accompanied a written application made by the agency for an international production order;  (c) a copy of each international production order issued in response to an application made by the agency;  (d) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under subclause 23(3);  (e) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under subclause 34(3);  (f) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under subclause 43(3);  (g) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under subclause 53(3);  (h) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under subclause 64(3);  (i) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under subclause 73(3);  (j) if the chief officer revokes an international production order under clause 114—a copy of the instrument of revocation.  (2) The period for which the chief officer of a relevant agency must cause a copy of a particular document to be kept in the agency’s records under subclause (1) is the period:  (a) starting when the document came into existence; and  (b) ending:  Schedule 1  International production orders" ;
    skos:definition "orders—relevant agencies  (1) The chief officer of a relevant agency must cause the following to be kept in the agency’s records:  (a) a copy of each written application made by the agency for an international production order;  (b) a copy of each affidavit that accompanied a written application made by the agency for an international production order;  (c) a copy of each international production order issued in response to an application made by the agency;  (d) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under subclause 23(3);  (e) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under subclause 34(3);  (f) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under subclause 43(3);  (g) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under subclause 53(3);  (h) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under subclause 64(3);  (i) a copy of each authorisation given by the chief officer under subclause 73(3);  (j) if the chief officer revokes an international production order under clause 114—a copy of the instrument of revocation.  (2) The period for which the chief officer of a relevant agency must cause a copy of a particular document to be kept in the agency’s records under subclause (1) is the period:  (a) starting when the document came into existence; and  (b) ending:  Schedule 1  International production orders"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "df6f616903150b9e38cf6aa07f5db4c534cea2ff4df909171568e0518fdf0ce8" ;
    cof:pageNumber "237"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-133-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-133-ss-2 ;
