concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-135-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "135(2) Keeping documents associated with international production"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-135-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) The period for which the Director-General of Security must cause a copy of a particular document to be kept in the Organisation’s records under subclause (1) is the period:  (a) starting when the document came into existence; and  (b) if:  (i) the document relates to an international production order that was issued under Part 4 of this Schedule; and  (ii) information was obtained in accordance with the order;  ending at the later of the following times:  (iii) when 3 years have elapsed since the document came into existence;  (iv) when the Organisation ceases to retain the information that was obtained in accordance with the order; and  (c) if paragraph (b) does not apply—ending when 3 years have elapsed since the document came into existence." ;
    skos:definition "(2) The period for which the Director-General of Security must cause a copy of a particular document to be kept in the Organisation’s records under subclause (1) is the period:  (a) starting when the document came into existence; and  (b) if:  (i) the document relates to an international production order that was issued under Part 4 of this Schedule; and  (ii) information was obtained in accordance with the order;  ending at the later of the following times:  (iii) when 3 years have elapsed since the document came into existence;  (iv) when the Organisation ceases to retain the information that was obtained in accordance with the order; and  (c) if paragraph (b) does not apply—ending when 3 years have elapsed since the document came into existence."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "4506234b7a9a7fc88c4f882253e864d798b99aa14ffa65f4bfba5bfaa903ea01" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-135 ;
    cof:pageNumber "240"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "The Organisation must keep a copy of the document for 3 years or until it ceases to retain information obtained in accordance with an international production order." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
