    cml:confidence "1.0000"^^xsd:decimal ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed .
doc:sch-1-sec-140-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "140(3) Destruction of records" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) If:  (a) an international production order was issued in response to an application made by a relevant agency; and  (b) in compliance with the order, a prescribed communications provider makes a copy of stored communications available to the agency (whether directly or indirectly via the Australian Designated Authority); and  (c) the copy is in the agency’s possession; and  (d) the chief officer of the agency is satisfied that the copy is not likely to be required for a purpose referred to in clause 153 or 158; the chief officer must cause the copy to be destroyed immediately after becoming so satisfied." ;
    cof:pageNumber "250"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-140-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "140(4) Destruction of records"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-140-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) If:  (a) an international production order was issued under clause 98; and  (b) in compliance with the order, a prescribed communications provider makes a copy of stored communications available to the Organisation (whether directly or indirectly via the Australian Designated Authority); and  (c) the copy is in the Organisation’s possession; and  Schedule 1  International production orders" ;
    skos:definition "(4) If:  (a) an international production order was issued under clause 98; and  (b) in compliance with the order, a prescribed communications provider makes a copy of stored communications available to the Organisation (whether directly or indirectly via the Australian Designated Authority); and  (c) the copy is in the Organisation’s possession; and  Schedule 1  International production orders"@en ;
