doc:sch-1-sec-143-ss-1 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "143(1) Inspection of records—Australian Designated Authority" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Ombudsman may inspect records of the Australian Designated Authority to determine the extent of compliance with this Schedule by the Australian Designated Authority." ;
    cof:pageNumber "254"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-143-ss-2 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "143(2) Inspection of records—Australian Designated Authority"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-143-ss-2 ;
    values:originalText "(2) For the purpose of an inspection under this clause, the Ombudsman:  (a) after notifying the Australian Designated Authority, may enter at any reasonable time premises occupied by the Attorney-General’s Department; and  (b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times to all records of the Australian Designated Authority that are relevant to the inspection; and  International production orders  Schedule 1 Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Part 10  Clause 144  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (c) despite any other law, is entitled to make copies of, and to take extracts from, records of the Australian Designated Authority; and  (d) may require a member of staff of the Attorney-General’s Department to give the Ombudsman any information that the Ombudsman considers necessary, being information:  (i) that is in the member’s possession, or to which the member has access; and  (ii) that is relevant to the inspection." ;
    skos:definition "(2) For the purpose of an inspection under this clause, the Ombudsman:  (a) after notifying the Australian Designated Authority, may enter at any reasonable time premises occupied by the Attorney-General’s Department; and  (b) is entitled to have full and free access at all reasonable times to all records of the Australian Designated Authority that are relevant to the inspection; and  International production orders  Schedule 1 Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Part 10  Clause 144  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (c) despite any other law, is entitled to make copies of, and to take extracts from, records of the Australian Designated Authority; and  (d) may require a member of staff of the Attorney-General’s Department to give the Ombudsman any information that the Ombudsman considers necessary, being information:  (i) that is in the member’s possession, or to which the member has access; and  (ii) that is relevant to the inspection."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "ea23b49d45b9168bbb93988466aedb6e10438d85434ec472dcd95f3d3bd2d90e" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-143 ;
