doc:sch-1-sec-146-ss-3 a cof:Section ;
    cof:title "146(3) Application of Ombudsman Act" ;
    values:kind "subsection" ;
    values:originalText "(3) Subject to clause 145, subsections 35(2), (3), (4) and (8) of the Ombudsman Act 1976 apply for the purposes of this Part and so apply as if:  International production orders  Schedule 1 Oversight by the Commonwealth Ombudsman  Part 10  Clause 147  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (a) a reference in those subsections to an officer were a reference to an inspecting officer; and  (b) a reference in those subsections to information did not include a reference to protected information; and  (c) a reference in those subsections to that Act were a reference to this Part; and  (d) paragraph 35(3)(b) of that Act were omitted; and  (e) section 35A of that Act had not been enacted." ;
    cof:pageNumber "258"^^xsd:integer .

concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-147 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "147 Exchange of information between Ombudsman or"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-147 ;
    values:originalText "Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security, and State/Territory inspecting authorities Exchange of information between Ombudsman and State/Territory inspecting authorities  (1) If the Ombudsman has obtained under this Part information relating to an authority of a State or Territory, the Ombudsman may give the information to another authority of that State or Territory (an inspecting authority) that:  (a) has powers under the law of that State or Territory; and  (b) has the function of making inspections of a similar kind to those provided for in clause 142 when the inspecting authority is exercising those powers.  (2) However, the Ombudsman may give the information only if the Ombudsman is satisfied that giving the information is necessary to enable the inspecting authority to perform its functions in relation to the first-mentioned authority of the State or Territory.  (3) An inspecting authority may give the Ombudsman information relevant to the performance of the Ombudsman’s functions under this Part.  Schedule 1  International production orders" ;
    skos:definition "Inspector-General of Intelligence and Security, and State/Territory inspecting authorities Exchange of information between Ombudsman and State/Territory inspecting authorities  (1) If the Ombudsman has obtained under this Part information relating to an authority of a State or Territory, the Ombudsman may give the information to another authority of that State or Territory (an inspecting authority) that:  (a) has powers under the law of that State or Territory; and  (b) has the function of making inspections of a similar kind to those provided for in clause 142 when the inspecting authority is exercising those powers.  (2) However, the Ombudsman may give the information only if the Ombudsman is satisfied that giving the information is necessary to enable the inspecting authority to perform its functions in relation to the first-mentioned authority of the State or Territory.  (3) An inspecting authority may give the Ombudsman information relevant to the performance of the Ombudsman’s functions under this Part.  Schedule 1  International production orders"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "31fbcbea5877e2bc019e6028a6e08d14efd101cbb1f1aec0f44a041ab3b35068" ;
    cof:pageNumber "259"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-147-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-147-ss-2 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-147-ss-3 ;
