concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-152 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "152 Prohibition on use, recording or disclosure of protected"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-152 ;
    values:originalText "information or its admission in evidence  (1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person uses, records or discloses information; and  (b) the information is protected information; and  (c) the use, recording or disclosure of the information is not permitted by this Part. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.  (2) Subject to this Part, protected information must not be admitted in evidence in any proceedings in Australia." ;
    skos:definition "information or its admission in evidence  (1) A person commits an offence if:  (a) the person uses, records or discloses information; and  (b) the information is protected information; and  (c) the use, recording or disclosure of the information is not permitted by this Part. Penalty: Imprisonment for 2 years.  (2) Subject to this Part, protected information must not be admitted in evidence in any proceedings in Australia."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "2952a24e6739c3fcf50ad7fd58db12fe3a7a5936119fe7234d70ffbf8fd174db" ;
    cof:pageNumber "263"^^xsd:integer ;
