    values:originalText "(1) A certifying officer of an interception agency may issue a written certificate signed by the officer setting out such facts as the officer considers relevant with respect to:  (a) the receipt by the agency of:  (i) intercepted communications; or  (ii) intercepted messages; or  (iii) intercepted voice calls; or  (iv) intercepted video calls;  that were made available to the agency in accordance with an international production order issued under clause 30; or  International production orders  Schedule 1 Evidentiary certificates  Part 12  Clause 163  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026  (b) the receipt by the agency of telecommunications data that was disclosed to the agency in accordance with an international production order issued under clause 30." ;
