concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-164-ss-3 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "164(3) Evidentiary certificates—stored communications"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-164-ss-3 ;
    values:originalText "(3) A certifying person may issue a written certificate signed by the person setting out such facts as the person considers relevant with respect to:  (a) the receipt by the Organisation of a copy of stored communications that were made available to the Organisation in accordance with an international production order issued under clause 98; or  (b) the receipt by the Organisation of telecommunications data that was disclosed to the Organisation in accordance with an international production order issued under clause 98.  International production orders  Schedule 1 Evidentiary certificates  Part 12  Clause 165  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026" ;
    skos:definition "(3) A certifying person may issue a written certificate signed by the person setting out such facts as the person considers relevant with respect to:  (a) the receipt by the Organisation of a copy of stored communications that were made available to the Organisation in accordance with an international production order issued under clause 98; or  (b) the receipt by the Organisation of telecommunications data that was disclosed to the Organisation in accordance with an international production order issued under clause 98.  International production orders  Schedule 1 Evidentiary certificates  Part 12  Clause 165  Telecommunications (Interception and Access) Act 1979  Compilation date: 04/06/2026"@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "94129a39fdd93d65293cff9e1e79008db59ac56ef2a1a5299b154c8efe6a8294" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-164 ;
