concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-164-ss-4 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "164(4) Evidentiary certificates—stored communications"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-164-ss-4 ;
    values:originalText "(4) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under subclause (1), (2) or (3):  (a) is to be received in evidence in a proceeding in Australia without further proof; and  (b) in a proceeding in Australia, is prima facie evidence of the matters stated in the document." ;
    skos:definition "(4) A document purporting to be a certificate issued under subclause (1), (2) or (3):  (a) is to be received in evidence in a proceeding in Australia without further proof; and  (b) in a proceeding in Australia, is prima facie evidence of the matters stated in the document."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "af9781850faadca17b7d08fce48688265745f499bc86dfc56318daf15ec408f1" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-164 ;
    cof:pageNumber "292"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Exhibit stored communication certificates as prima facie evidence in Australian proceedings." ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
