concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-172-ss-5 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "172(5) International production order issued in response to a telephone"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-172-ss-5 ;
    values:originalText "(5) If the international production order is cancelled by the issuing person under subclause (3):  (a) the issuing person must:  (i) give the instrument of cancellation to the Australian Designated Authority; and  (ii) do so as soon as practicable after the order is cancelled; and  (b) if the telephone application was made on behalf of a relevant agency—the Australian Designated Authority must:  (i) inform the chief officer of the relevant agency of the cancellation; and  (ii) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of cancellation is given to the Australian Designated Authority; and  (c) if the telephone application was made on behalf of the Organisation—the Australian Designated Authority must:  (i) inform the Organisation of the cancellation; and  (ii) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of cancellation is given to the Australian Designated Authority." ;
    skos:definition "(5) If the international production order is cancelled by the issuing person under subclause (3):  (a) the issuing person must:  (i) give the instrument of cancellation to the Australian Designated Authority; and  (ii) do so as soon as practicable after the order is cancelled; and  (b) if the telephone application was made on behalf of a relevant agency—the Australian Designated Authority must:  (i) inform the chief officer of the relevant agency of the cancellation; and  (ii) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of cancellation is given to the Australian Designated Authority; and  (c) if the telephone application was made on behalf of the Organisation—the Australian Designated Authority must:  (i) inform the Organisation of the cancellation; and  (ii) do so as soon as practicable after the instrument of cancellation is given to the Australian Designated Authority."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "f05d7fb8f4ffd8bcaf8410e9acfbdce57ae9112b6bea9d5003405872986d7a2e" ;
    values:partOf concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-172 ;
    cof:pageNumber "300"^^xsd:integer ;
    skos:note "Must inform relevant parties of cancellation" ;
    dc:description "instrument of cancellation" ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
    cml:proposedBy <https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml> ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979.pdf> ;
