concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-179 a cml:Concept ;
    skos:prefLabel "179 Delegation by the Australian Designated Authority"@en ;
    cml:realizedBy doc:sch-1-sec-179 ;
    values:originalText "(1) The Australian Designated Authority may, by writing, delegate any or all of the Australian Designated Authority’s functions or powers under this Schedule to:  (a) an SES employee, or acting SES employee, in the Attorney-General’s Department; or  (b) an APS employee who holds, or is acting in, an Executive Level 1 or 2 position in the Attorney-General’s Department. Note: The expressions SES employee, acting SES employee and APS employee are defined in section 2B of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  (2) In performing functions, or exercising powers, under a delegation under subclause (1), the delegate must comply with any directions of the Australian Designated Authority." ;
    skos:definition "(1) The Australian Designated Authority may, by writing, delegate any or all of the Australian Designated Authority’s functions or powers under this Schedule to:  (a) an SES employee, or acting SES employee, in the Attorney-General’s Department; or  (b) an APS employee who holds, or is acting in, an Executive Level 1 or 2 position in the Attorney-General’s Department. Note: The expressions SES employee, acting SES employee and APS employee are defined in section 2B of the Acts Interpretation Act 1901.  (2) In performing functions, or exercising powers, under a delegation under subclause (1), the delegate must comply with any directions of the Australian Designated Authority."@en ;
    cml:integrityHash "34ab8fc0be392aad41d1ae852b1e32edfb1eade1fea0caf749a2299585831e03" ;
    cof:pageNumber "306"^^xsd:integer ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-179-ss-1 ;
    cml:hasPart concept:telecommunications-interception-and-access-act-1979-sch-1-sec-179-ss-2 ;
    cml:curationStatus cml:Proposed ;
    cml:schemaVersion "2" ;
